Read.me Items for Windows 3.1 and/or Windows NT Configuration of MACHXL

1. If you haven't already done so,
   install Windows 3.1 or Windows NT.

2. If you haven't already done so,
   install MACHXL.

3. Be sure that both C:\WINDOWS & C:\MACHXL\EXE (or your selected path)
   are in the path statement in your AUTOEXEC.BAT file.

4. Re-boot the computer.

5. Run Windows

6. From within windows, do these operations:
        a. Go into the File Manager.
        b. Select the Machxl\Dat directory.
        c. Drag the Machxl.pif (or for NT the Machxlnt.pif) file
           into the window from which you would like to run
           Machxl. (eg. Main)
        d. Click once on the Machxl (Machxlnt) icon.
        e. Select FILE/PROPERTIES.
        f. Verify that the Description reads Machxl or Machxlnt.
        g. Verify that the Command Line contains the correct path to
           Machxl\Dat\Machxl(nt).pif.
        h. Verify that the Working Directory shows C:\Machxl\Dat (or the
           path where Machxl was installed).
        i. Select Change Icon/Browse and select the path to Machxl\Dat.
        j. Select ~AMD.ICO and OK.
        k. Select OK to leave the Change Icon box.
        l. The AMD icon should now show in the Program Item
           Properties box.
        m. Select OK to leave the box.

   Note: If you have installed Machxl on a drive other than C:\
         you must also modify the .pif file. To do so follow
         these steps:
                a. Select Main/Pif editor.
                b. Select File/Open.
                c. Select the drive and path to Machxl\dat
                d. Select the appropriate .pif file (machxl or machxlnt).
                e. Change the path under "Program Filename" to reflect
                   where Machxl is installed.
                f. Change "Start-up Directory" to reflect the appropriate
                   drive. (eg. d:\)
                g. Select File/Save
                h. Select File/Close

6. Test the MACHXL installation by "double-clicking" on the icon.
        Machxl will start-up using the examples directory the first time,
        but will remember the last "current directory" when
        you end a MACHXL session.

